</section>
<section id="A5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.3 </span>Models</h3>

<section id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Urban locomotion.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In urban locomotion, the embodied AI agent controls the robot’s locomotion, ensuring stable and efficient movement across various terrains such as flat surfaces, slopes, and stairs.
The input is an elevation map, sensorimotor signals (such as joint positions, velocities, and torques), and velocity commands from the navigation module. The output is low-level control signals (such as joint positions and wheel velocity), which a controller then translates into actual motor commands that drive the robot’s actuators.
We learn four locomotion models on different subsets – Urban-Loc-i-Train (j=1,2,3,4), as well as a general locomotion model in the mixed terrains, which will be used in Human-AI-Mode-2 in the urban traverse benchmark.
For each model, the focus is to match the target velocity command from the navigation module while keeping balance on the terrain.
We model locomotion as a reinforcement learning problem, where the AI learns an optimal locomotion policy <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\text{loc}}^{j}(s)\in\Pi_{\text{loc}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mtext>loc</mtext><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>loc</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\text{loc}}^{j}(s)\in\Pi_{\text{loc}}</annotation></semantics></math> through PPO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib63" title="" class="ltx_ref">63</a>]</cite>.
The locomotion policy is trained to maximize rewards that prioritize smooth, stable movement:</p>
<table id="A5.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi_{\text{loc}}^{j*}(s)=\arg\max_{\pi_{\text{loc}}^{j}}\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{t=0}^{T}\gamma^{t}r_{\text{loc}}^{j}(s_{t},a_{t})\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mtext>loc</mtext><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>arg</mi><munder><mi>max</mi><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mtext>loc</mtext><mi>j</mi></msubsup></munder><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mtext>loc</mtext><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\text{loc}}^{j*}(s)=\arg\max_{\pi_{\text{loc}}^{j}}\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{t=0}^{T}\gamma^{t}r_{\text{loc}}^{j}(s_{t},a_{t})\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\text{loc}}^{j}(s_{t},a_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mtext>loc</mtext><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\text{loc}}^{j}(s_{t},a_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> is the reward function for locomotion, which provides rewards for maintaining balance, smooth movement, and energy efficiency, penalties are applied for unsafe actions (<em id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">e.g</em>.<span id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text"></span>, stumbling or wasting energy); <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>: The state of the robot’s body at time <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>; The locomotion action at time <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> – low-level control signals to drive robot’s actuators; <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>: controls the balance between immediate rewards and long-term rewards.
Finally, we can get a set of primitive locomotion policies, each of which excels in maintaining stability on one specific terrain when advancing toward the target point.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Urban navigation.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In urban navigation, the embodied AI agent handles local navigation, determining how the robot should move to stay within traversable areas while avoiding obstacles and pedestrians.
The input is RGBD frames, the current coordinate of the agent, and the coordinate of the target point. The output is the target linear and angular velocity command.
We learn three navigation models on different subsets – Urban-Nav-j-Train (j=1,2,3).
For each policy, the goal is to maximize both efficiency and safety while progressing toward the goal. This problem is modeled as a Markov Decision Process (MDP) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">60</a>]</cite>, where the AI learns to optimize its navigation policy <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\text{nav}}^{i}(s)\in\Pi_{\text{nav}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mtext>nav</mtext><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>nav</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\text{nav}}^{i}(s)\in\Pi_{\text{nav}}</annotation></semantics></math> using Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib63" title="" class="ltx_ref">63</a>]</cite>, a reinforcement learning method.
The navigation policy is trained to maximize the expected cumulative rewards:</p>
<table id="A5.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi_{\text{nav}}^{i*}(s)=\arg\max_{\pi_{\text{nav}}^{i}}\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{t=0}^{T}\gamma^{t}r_{\text{nav}}^{i}(s_{t},a_{t})\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mtext>nav</mtext><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>arg</mi><munder><mi>max</mi><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mtext>nav</mtext><mi>i</mi></msubsup></munder><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mtext>nav</mtext><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\text{nav}}^{i*}(s)=\arg\max_{\pi_{\text{nav}}^{i}}\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{t=0}^{T}\gamma^{t}r_{\text{nav}}^{i}(s_{t},a_{t})\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\text{nav}}^{i}(s_{t},a_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mtext>nav</mtext><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\text{nav}}^{i}(s_{t},a_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>: The reward function for navigation, providing positive rewards for progress towards the target and safe navigation (<em id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">e.g</em>.<span id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text"></span>, avoiding obstacles), while penalizing collisions or inefficiency; <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>: The state of the robot at time <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>: The navigation action at time <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> – the linear and angular velocity of robot. <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> controls the balance between immediate rewards and long-term rewards.
With the optimization of policies, we can finally get a set of primitive navigation policies, each of which is an expert in dealing with one specific navigation scenario.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Urban traverse.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In urban traverse, humans and AI cooperate to complete the kilometer-scale task. Humans need to make a decision that involves determining whether the human or AI should control the robot based on the observed conditions (terrain and obstacle types) of the next interval. The interval can be split by geodesic distance or time duration.
The process is split into two main decisions: 1) whether the human supervisor should take over or let the AI continue, and 2) if the AI is in control, selecting the best combination of navigation and locomotion experts.
The decision-making process can be expressed as:</p>
<table id="A5.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\text{system}}^{*}(s_{k})=\begin{cases}\pi_{h}(s_{k})&amp;\text{if }h_{k}=1,\\
\left(\pi_{\text{nav}}^{i^{*}},\pi_{\text{loc}}^{j^{*}}\right)&amp;\text{if }h_{k}=0,\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mtext>system</mtext><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mtext>nav</mtext><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mtext>loc</mtext><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\text{system}}^{*}(s_{k})=\begin{cases}\pi_{h}(s_{k})&amp;\text{if }h_{k}=1,\\
\left(\pi_{\text{nav}}^{i^{*}},\pi_{\text{loc}}^{j^{*}}\right)&amp;\text{if }h_{k}=0,\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is the current <span id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">state</span> of the system at decision point <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is a binary variable representing whether human control is selected (<math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{k}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{k}=1</annotation></semantics></math>) or AI control is maintained (<math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{k}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{k}=0</annotation></semantics></math>); <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{h}(s_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{h}(s_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> represents the human control policy; <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\text{nav}}^{i^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mtext>nav</mtext><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\text{nav}}^{i^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the selected primitive navigation policy from the set <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\text{nav}}=\{\pi_{\text{nav}}^{1},\pi_{\text{nav}}^{2},\dots,\pi_{\text{nav}}^{N_{\text{nav}}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>nav</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mtext>nav</mtext><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mtext>nav</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mtext>nav</mtext><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>nav</mtext></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\text{nav}}=\{\pi_{\text{nav}}^{1},\pi_{\text{nav}}^{2},\dots,\pi_{\text{nav}}^{N_{\text{nav}}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\text{loc}}^{j^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mtext>loc</mtext><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\text{loc}}^{j^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the selected primitive locomotion policy from the set <math id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\text{loc}}=\{\pi_{\text{loc}}^{1},\pi_{\text{loc}}^{2},\dots,\pi_{\text{loc}}^{N_{\text{loc}}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mtext>loc</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mtext>loc</mtext><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mtext>loc</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mtext>loc</mtext><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>loc</mtext></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\text{loc}}=\{\pi_{\text{loc}}^{1},\pi_{\text{loc}}^{2},\dots,\pi_{\text{loc}}^{N_{\text{loc}}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For the urban traverse task, based on the foundational models, we construct 4 different control modes, spanning from fully human to fully AI as below.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline ltx_font_italic">1) Human.</span> A fully human control mode. Humans control a robot’s navigation to make waypoint following. The robot uses a general locomotion model trained on mixed terrain.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline ltx_font_italic">2) AI.</span> A fully AI control model. The robot uses a general navigation model to make waypoint following and a general locomotion model to traverse terrains.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline ltx_font_italic">4) Human-AI-Mode-1.</span> A human AI shared control mode. Humans dispatch foundational navigation models and locomotion models based on scene conditions at every decision point or call humans for takeover.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline ltx_font_italic">3) Human-AI-Mode-2.</span> A human AI shared control mode. Humans dispatch foundational navigation models and the general locomotion model based on scene conditions at every decision point or call humans for takeover.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.4 </span>Navigation Benchmark</h3>

<div id="A5.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we will describe the experiment in detail regarding the task of navigation.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Environments.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">There are three environments, i.e., NavClear, NavStatic and NavDynamic. For experiments on NavClear, there is nothing except the ego agent in the environment. The agent needs to move from the starting point to the destination, given the location of the ending point. We train the agent on <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10m\times 10m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10m\times 10m</annotation></semantics></math>
regions with different textures of the walkable and non-walkable regions. To evaluate the trained policy, we generate <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="15m\times 15m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>15</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">15m\times 15m</annotation></semantics></math> regions with the same textures as the training domain.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For experiments on NavStatic, there are only static objects except the ego agent in the environment. The agent needs to move from the starting point to the destination, given the location of the ending point, and it should collide with any other objects as little as possible. We train the agent on <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10m\times 10m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10m\times 10m</annotation></semantics></math>
regions with different textures of the walkable and non-walkable regions and <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> objects. To evaluate the trained policy, we generate <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="15m\times 15m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>15</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">15m\times 15m</annotation></semantics></math> regions with the same textures as the training domain and <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math> objects.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For experiments on NavDynamic, there are not only static objects but also dynamic pedestrians, except the ego agent, in the environment. The agent needs to move from the starting point to the destination, given the location of the ending point, and it should collide with any other objects as little as possible. We train the agent on <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10m\times 10m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10m\times 10m</annotation></semantics></math>
regions with different textures of the walkable and non-walkable regions, <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> objects, and <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> pedestrians. To evaluate the trained policy, we generate <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="15m\times 15m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>15</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">15m\times 15m</annotation></semantics></math> regions with the same textures as the training domain, <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math> objects, and <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> pedestrians.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Action spaces.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use the action that is a 2-dimension vector normalized to <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-1.0,1.0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-1.0,1.0]</annotation></semantics></math>, where the two components indicate the relative proportions of the max velocity in the <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x-</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y-</annotation></semantics></math> directions. It would be processed by the locomotion model for Unitree robots or the Ackermann model for the COCO robot to generate the final action as input of the physics model.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Observation spaces.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Multi-model observations are used in all robots for training, including RGB and depth images with the resolution of <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="128\times 128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>128</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">128\times 128</annotation></semantics></math>, the vector indicating the localization and the destination, the projected velocity on the target direction, and the height map in the region of <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.6m\times 1.0m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1.6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.6m\times 1.0m</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Methods.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In our study, we employ the Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib63" title="" class="ltx_ref">63</a>]</cite> to train the policy for all agents. PPO is a widely adopted and effective method, and it is easy to scale by
adopting parallel and distributed training. It took about 8, 18, and 24 hours to train the model on a single Nvidia L40S GPU for NavClear, NavStatic, and NavDynamic, respectively. The detailed hyperparameters are provided in Table <a href="#A5.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ Rewards. ‣ E.5 Locomotion Benchmark ‣ Appendix E URBAN-BENCH Experimental Details ‣ Towards Autonomous Micromobility through Scalable Urban Simulation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A5.T5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 5</span>: </span><span id="A5.T5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Hyper-parameters of RL in urban navigation.</span></figcaption>
<table id="A5.T5.6" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A5.T5.6.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T5.6.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"><span id="A5.T5.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">PPO Hyper-parameters</span></td>
<td id="A5.T5.6.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"><span id="A5.T5.6.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Value</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T5.6.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T5.6.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Environmental horizon <math id="A5.T5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A5.T5.6.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">200</td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T5.6.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T5.6.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Learning rate</td>
<td id="A5.T5.6.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">4e-4</td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T5.6.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T5.6.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Discount factor <math id="A5.T5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A5.T5.6.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">0.99</td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T5.6.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T5.6.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">GAE parameter <math id="A5.T5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A5.T5.6.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">0.95</td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T5.6.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T5.6.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Clip parameter <math id="A5.T5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A5.T5.6.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">0.2</td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T5.6.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T5.6.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Train batch size</td>
<td id="A5.T5.6.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A5.T5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="256\times 60(n_{env}\times n_{step})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>256</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>60</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">256\times 60(n_{env}\times n_{step})</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T5.6.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T5.6.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">SGD minibatch size</td>
<td id="A5.T5.6.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">3840</td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T5.6.9" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T5.6.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Value loss coefficient</td>
<td id="A5.T5.6.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">1.0</td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T5.6.10" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T5.6.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">Entropy loss coefficient</td>
<td id="A5.T5.6.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">0.0005</td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Rewards.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The reward function is composed as follows:</p>
<table id="A5.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=R_{term}+c_{1}R_{track}+c_{2}R_{walkable}+c_{3}R_{collision}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=R_{term}+c_{1}R_{track}+c_{2}R_{walkable}+c_{3}R_{collision}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<ul id="A5.I1" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Terminal reward <math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{term}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{term}</annotation></semantics></math>:
a sparse reward set to <math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+50</annotation></semantics></math> if the vehicle reaches the destination, and <math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-100</annotation></semantics></math> for out of boundaries. If given <math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{term}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{term}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> at any time step <math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, the episode will be terminated at <math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> immediately.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Tracking reward <math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{track}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{track}</annotation></semantics></math>: a dense reward defined as <math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R_{track}=[1-torch.tanh(d_{s-2-d}/1.0)]+0.2*[1-torch.tanh(d_{s-2-d}/0.2)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>1.0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0.2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>0.2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{track}=[1-torch.tanh(d_{s-2-d}/1.0)]+0.2*[1-torch.tanh(d_{s-2-d}/0.2)]</annotation></semantics></math>, wherein the <math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{s-2-d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{s-2-d}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the distance between the location and the destination. We set the weight of <math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{track}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{track}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}=2.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}=2.0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">On-walkable-region reward <math id="A5.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{walkable}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{walkable}</annotation></semantics></math>: a dense reward defined as <math id="A5.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{walkable}=-1_{non-walkable}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{walkable}=-1_{non-walkable}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, wherein the <math id="A5.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1_{non-walkable}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1_{non-walkable}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes that the agent walks on non-walkable regions at time <math id="A5.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. We set the weight of <math id="A5.I1.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{walkable}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{walkable}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A5.I1.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Collision reward <math id="A5.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{collision}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{collision}</annotation></semantics></math>: a dense negative reward defined as <math id="A5.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-1(c_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-1(c_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, wherein the <math id="A5.I1.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the collision between agents and any other objects at time <math id="A5.I1.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.I1.i4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is the indicator function. We set the weight of <math id="A5.I1.i4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{crash}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{crash}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A5.I1.i4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{3}=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{3}=1.0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.5 </span>Locomotion Benchmark</h3>

<div id="A5.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we will describe the experiment in detail regarding the task of locomotion.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS5.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Environments.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">There are several environments, <em id="A5.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">i.e</em>.<span id="A5.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text"></span>, LocoFlat, LocoSlope, LocoStair, LocoRough, and general environment. Each environment has a specific type of terrain, and the general one has all types of terrain. We provide details of the environments for locomotion training in Table <a href="#A5.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ E.1 Data ‣ Appendix E URBAN-BENCH Experimental Details ‣ Towards Autonomous Micromobility through Scalable Urban Simulation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS5.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Action spaces.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The action space is specifically given by the URDF file of the robot; there are 12, 16, and 37 joints for go2, g1, and b2w, respectively.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS5.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Observation spaces.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Multi-model observations are used in all robots for training, including linear velocity, angular velocity, target velocity, joint position, joint velocity, latest action, and the height map in the region of <math id="A5.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.6m\times 1.0m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1.6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.6m\times 1.0m</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS5.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Methods.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Like the navigation benchmark, we employ the Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib63" title="" class="ltx_ref">63</a>]</cite> to train the policy for all agents. PPO is a widely adopted and effective method, and it is easy to scale by
adopting parallel and distributed training. It took about 8, 18, and 24 hours to train the model on a single Nvidia L40S GPU for NavClear, NavStatic, and NavDynamic, respectively. The detailed hyperparameters are provided in Table <a href="#A5.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ Rewards. ‣ E.5 Locomotion Benchmark ‣ Appendix E URBAN-BENCH Experimental Details ‣ Towards Autonomous Micromobility through Scalable Urban Simulation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS5.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Rewards.</h4>

<div id="A5.SS5.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS5.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The reward function is composed as follows:</p>
<table id="A5.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=R_{term}+c_{1}R_{track}+c_{2}R_{vel}+c_{3}R_{smooth}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=R_{term}+c_{1}R_{track}+c_{2}R_{vel}+c_{3}R_{smooth}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<ul id="A5.I2" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A5.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Terminal reward <math id="A5.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{term}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{term}</annotation></semantics></math>: a sparse reward set to <math id="A5.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-100</annotation></semantics></math> is needed for situations where there is a contact force <math id="A5.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;1.0</annotation></semantics></math> between the agent and the ground. If given <math id="A5.I2.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{term}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{term}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> at any time step <math id="A5.I2.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, the episode will be terminated at <math id="A5.I2.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> immediately.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Tracking reward <math id="A5.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{track}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{track}</annotation></semantics></math>: a dense reward defined as <math id="A5.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R_{track}=\exp(-\delta v/0.25**2)+0.5\times\exp(-\delta z/0.25**2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>δ</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>0.25</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>δ</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>0.25</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{track}=\exp(-\delta v/0.25**2)+0.5\times\exp(-\delta z/0.25**2)</annotation></semantics></math>, wherein the <math id="A5.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta v</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the error between the current velocity and target velocity. We set the weight of <math id="A5.I2.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{track}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{track}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A5.I2.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}=1.0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">On-walkable-region reward <math id="A5.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{vel}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{vel}</annotation></semantics></math>: a dense reward defined as <math id="A5.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{vel}=-v_{z}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{vel}=-v_{z}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, wherein the <math id="A5.I2.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{z}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes along the <math id="A5.I2.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z-</annotation></semantics></math>axis. We set the weight of <math id="A5.I2.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{walkable}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{walkable}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A5.I2.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}=2.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}=2.0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Collision reward <math id="A5.I2.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{smooth}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{smooth}</annotation></semantics></math>: a dense negative reward defined as <math id="A5.I2.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-||a(t)-a(t-1)||_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-||a(t)-a(t-1)||_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, wherein the <math id="A5.I2.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a(t)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the action of the agent at time <math id="A5.I2.i4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> . We set the weight of <math id="A5.I2.i4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{crash}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{crash}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A5.I2.i4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{3}=0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{3}=0.01</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
